Day 200: A^{(2)} vs p_2(Y) test

STRATEGY:
  Bullet action of Y_i raises degree by 1, so p_2(Y) raises degree by 2.
  An operator that raises degree cannot have any single-degree eigenvector.
  Therefore in the raw bullet action, p_2(Y) is NOT diagonalized by any
  fixed-degree Macdonald basis.  The identification A^{(2)} = c(q,t) p_2(Y)
  as OPERATORS ON Sym_{q,t} in the bullet action is refuted by degree alone.
  The identification only makes sense after applying Hikita's isomorphism
  Sym_{q,t} ~= Lambda_{q,t} that sends bullet action of Y to ⋆-multiplication,
  in which case the ⋆-eigenvalue of (p_2(Y).1) should match c(q,t) * A^{(2)}-eigval.

